IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-part03-general-provisions`

-- Tests for Part 3 (qld-part03-general-provisions.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.

§ `Tests of Part 3`

§§ `s 9`

#ASSERT `an Act is interpreted as operating to the full extent of, but not to exceed, Parliament's legislative power (s 9(1)(a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is interpreted as operating to the full extent of, but not to exceed, Parliament's legislative power (s 9(1)(a))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act is interpreted as operating distributively (s 9(1)(b))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is interpreted as operating distributively (s 9(1)(b))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the declaration about the Coastal Waters Acts (Cwlth) applies and always applied (s 9(1A))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the declaration about the Coastal Waters Acts (Cwlth) applies and always applied (s 9(1A))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1B): "does not apply" in relation to the criminal law under the cooperative scheme: a flat negative.
#ASSERT `the declaration in s 9(1A) applies to the matter (s 9(1B))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the declaration in s 9(1A) applies to the matter (s 9(1B))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- SAYS A provision of an Act that would apart from s 9 be interpreted as exceeding power has effect to the extent to which it does not exceed power, and the remainder of the Act is not affected (s 9(2)).
#ASSERT `the provision has effect to the extent to which it does not exceed power (s 9(2)(a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the provision has effect to the extent to which it does not exceed power (s 9(2)(a))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the remainder of the Act is affected (s 9(2)(b))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the remainder of the Act is affected (s 9(2)(b))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the provision's application to other persons, matters or circumstances is affected (s 9(3))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the provision's application to other persons, matters or circumstances is affected (s 9(3))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9 applies to an Act in addition to, and without limiting, any provision of the Act (s 9(4))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9 applies to an Act in addition to, and without limiting, any provision of the Act (s 9(4))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 9A to 11`

#ASSERT `the provision has the same effect as it would have had, and is as valid as it would have been, if the Australia Acts had been in operation (s 9A)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the provision has the same effect as it would have had, and is as valid as it would have been, if the Australia Acts had been in operation (s 9A)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a section has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words (s 10)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a section has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words (s 10)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- SAYS An Act passed on 26 July 1852 itself is not within the words "after 26 July 1852", so s 11 does not answer for it (s 11).
-- s 11: "Every Act passed after 26 July 1852 is a public Act unless the Act otherwise expressly provides."
#ASSERT `an Act is a public Act (s 11)` (Date 27 7 1852) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is a public Act (s 11)` (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day itself is not "after" 26 July 1852
#ASSERT `an Act is a public Act (s 11)` (Date 26 7 1852) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act is a public Act (s 11)` (Date 1 1 1850) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the "unless" once met: the section no longer answers
#ASSERT `an Act is a public Act (s 11)` (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 12 and 12A`

-- s 12: a "private Act" does not (a) affect pre-existing rights prejudicially or (b) impose liabilities for earlier acts, except where it expressly provides, or (2) for those at whose instance it is passed.
#ASSERT `a private Act does the thing (s 12)` TRUE `affect pre-existing rights in a way prejudicial to the Crown or another person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a private Act does the thing (s 12)` TRUE `impose liabilities on the Crown or another person in relation to previous acts or omissions` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a private Act does the thing (s 12)` TRUE `affect pre-existing rights in a way prejudicial to the Crown or another person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a private Act does the thing (s 12)` TRUE `affect pre-existing rights in a way prejudicial to the Crown or another person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a private Act does the thing (s 12)` TRUE `anything else` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a private Act does the thing (s 12)` FALSE `affect pre-existing rights in a way prejudicial to the Crown or another person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a private Act has become a public Act merely because it was amended by or under a public Act (s 12A)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a private Act has become a public Act merely because it was amended by or under a public Act (s 12A)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a private Act has become a public Act merely because it was amended by or under a public Act (s 12A)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 13, 13A and 13B`

-- SAYS An Act passed after the commencement of this Act does not bind the Crown or derogate from a prerogative right of the Crown unless express words are included (s 13).
-- s 13: no Act passed after the commencement of this Act binds the Crown unless express words are included.
#ASSERT `the Act binds the Crown or derogates from a prerogative right of the Crown (s 13)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act binds the Crown or derogates from a prerogative right of the Crown (s 13)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Act binds the Crown or derogates from a prerogative right of the Crown (s 13)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13A(1): "only so far as it expressly provides"
#ASSERT `an Act affects native title (s 13A(1))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act affects native title (s 13A(1))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act affects native title (s 13A(1))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act affects native title for s 13A(1) (s 13A(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act affects native title for s 13A(1) (s 13A(2))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act affects native title for s 13A(1) (s 13A(2))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities of the Legislative Assembly or of its members or committees (s 13B(1))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities of the Legislative Assembly or of its members or committees (s 13B(1))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities of the Legislative Assembly or of its members or committees (s 13B(1))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities mentioned in s 13B(1) (s 13B(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities mentioned in s 13B(1) (s 13B(2))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `rights in s 13B includes privileges (s 13B(3))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `rights in s 13B includes privileges (s 13B(3))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 14`

-- SAYS A heading to a section is part of an Act enacted on or before 30 June 1991 only if the heading was amended or inserted after 30 June 1991; a footnote, editor's note or endnote is never part of the Act (s 14(2), (4)).
-- (2): a heading to a section is part of the Act if the Act is enacted after 30 June 1991 or the heading is amended or inserted after that date.
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `a heading to a section, subsection or another provision` (Date 1 7 1991) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `a heading to a section, subsection or another provision` (Date 30 6 1991) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `a heading to a section, subsection or another provision` (Date 30 6 1991) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `a heading to a chapter, part, division or subdivision` (Date 1 1 1954) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `an example of the operation of a provision` (Date 1 1 1954) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `a note to the Act or to a provision of the Act` (Date 1 1 1954) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `a schedule or appendix` (Date 1 1 1954) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `punctuation` (Date 1 1 1954) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` `a footnote or editor's note to an Act or provision, or an endnote to an Act` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 14A and 14B`

#ASSERT `the interpretation is to be preferred to any other interpretation (s 14A(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the interpretation is to be preferred to any other interpretation (s 14A(1))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14A(1) applies (s 14A(2))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14A(1) applies (s 14A(2))` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14A(1) creates or extends criminal liability (s 14A(2))` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14A applies to the Act despite any presumption or rule of interpretation (s 14A(3))` (Date 1 7 1991) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14A applies to the Act despite any presumption or rule of interpretation (s 14A(3))` (Date 30 6 1991) EQUALS NOTHING

-- SAYS Consideration may be given to extrinsic material to confirm the ordinary meaning only in a case that is neither ambiguous or obscure nor leads to a manifestly absurd or unreasonable result (s 14B(1)(c)).
-- s 14B(1): the three purposes.
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` `to provide an interpretation of a provision that is ambiguous or obscure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` `to provide an interpretation of a provision that is ambiguous or obscure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` `to provide an interpretation that avoids a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` `to provide an interpretation that avoids a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c) "in any other case"
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning of the provision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning of the provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning of the provision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (count (`the matters to which regard is to be had in deciding whether to consider extrinsic material and what weight to give it (s 14B(2))`)) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT elem OF `other relevant matters`, (`the matters to which regard is to be had in deciding whether to consider extrinsic material and what weight to give it (s 14B(2))`)
-- (3): "extrinsic material means relevant material not forming part of the Act concerned"
#ASSERT `the material is extrinsic material (s 14B(3))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is extrinsic material (s 14B(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the material is extrinsic material (s 14B(3))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- SAYS Extrinsic material means relevant material not forming part of the Act concerned (s 14B(3)).
#ASSERT `the kind of material is given as an example of extrinsic material (s 14B(3)(a) to (h))` `the speech made to the Legislative Assembly by the member when introducing the Bill` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kind of material is given as an example of extrinsic material (s 14B(3)(a) to (h))` `any other material` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the meaning is the ordinary meaning (s 14B(3), definition ordinary meaning)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the meaning is the ordinary meaning (s 14B(3), definition ordinary meaning)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 14C to 14D`

#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different words are used (s 14C)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different words are used (s 14C)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the absence of an express provision limits or affects an obligation to comply with procedural fairness implied under the general law (s 14CA(1))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the absence of an express provision limits or affects an obligation to comply with procedural fairness implied under the general law (s 14CA(1))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the absence of an express provision limits or affects an obligation to perform the function or exercise the power reasonably implied under the general law (s 14CA(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the absence of an express provision limits or affects an obligation to perform the function or exercise the power reasonably implied under the general law (s 14CA(2))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a former provision is replaced by a corresponding provision (s 14CA(3))` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a former provision is replaced by a corresponding provision (s 14CA(3))` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a former provision is replaced by a corresponding provision (s 14CA(3))` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a former provision is replaced by a corresponding provision (s 14CA(3))` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a provision is a corresponding provision to another provision (s 14CA(4))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision is a corresponding provision to another provision (s 14CA(4))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- SAYS If an example and the provision, read in context, are inconsistent, the provision prevails over the example (s 14D(c)).
#ASSERT `which prevails, the example or the provision (s 14D(c))` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the provision prevails`
#ASSERT `which prevails, the example or the provision (s 14D(c))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an example is exhaustive (s 14D(a))` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an example limits the meaning of the provision (s 14D(b))` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an example extends the meaning of the provision (s 14D(b))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an example extends the meaning of the provision (s 14D(b))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
